BEGIN_PGML Use DESMOS or some other graphing calculator to graph each pair of expressions. Do they appear to be equivalent? (For those that appear equivalent, can you prove that they are? For example by using trigonometric identities?)
a. [`\csc^2 \left(\frac{x}{2}\right) + \sec^2 \left(\frac{x}{2}\right)`] and [`4\csc^2 x`]
[_]{$radio1}{5}
a. [`\sqrt{3}\cos x+\sin x`] and [`2\cos\left(x-2.18\pi\right)`]
[_]{$radio2}{5}
a. [`\csc (2x)`] and [`\sec(x) \csc(x)`]
[_]{$radio3}{5}
a. [`\csc (2x)`] and [`\frac{\sec(x) \csc(x)}{2}`]
[_]{$radio4}{5}
END_PGML
